#: btmanager.lua:536
msgid ""
"Bluetooth firmware files are missing.\n"
"\n"
"Your Kobo's Bluetooth chip needs to be initialized by the stock Kobo OS (Nickel) before it can be used in KOReader.\n"
"\n"
"To fix this:\n"
"1. Fully power off your Kobo\n"
"2. Turn it on and boot normally into Nickel\n"
"3. Go to Settings → Bluetooth and turn it ON\n"
"4. If you have Bluetooth headphones, pair them now\n"
"5. Once Bluetooth is working in Nickel, reboot into KOReader\n"
"\n"
"This one-time setup is needed because the Bluetooth firmware configuration is written by Nickel's startup process and is not preserved across KOReader-only reboots."
msgstr ""
"Faltan archivos de firmware Bluetooth.\n"
"\n"
"El chip Bluetooth de su Kobo debe ser inicializado por el sistema operativo Kobo original (Nickel) antes de poder usarlo en KOReader.\n"
"\n"
"Para solucionar esto:\n"
"1. Apague completamente su Kobo\n"
"2. Enciéndelo y arranca normalmente en Nickel\n"
"3. Vaya a Configuración → Bluetooth y actívelo.\n"
"4. Si tienes auriculares Bluetooth, emparéjalos ahora\n"
"5. Una vez que Bluetooth esté funcionando en Nickel, reinicie en KOReader\n"
"\n"
"Esta configuración única es necesaria porque la configuración del firmware Bluetooth se escribe mediante el proceso de inicio de Nickel y no se conserva en los reinicios solo de KOReader."

